WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.027
A reshape is more reversible when each source value maps cleanly to one output cell and category labels

00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:12.467
are preserved. It becomes lossy when several rows are aggregated into one cell.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.512
Dropping NULL rows can also remove missingness information.

00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:19.757
Collapsing categories can remove distinctions.

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:23.897
Always identify which information survives the transformation.

00:00:23.897 --> 00:00:32.107
A reshape is reversible only when the transformation preserves enough information to reconstruct the source.

00:00:32.107 --> 00:00:37.192
Aggregation, duplicate collapsing, and dropped NULL cells can make the process lossy.

00:00:37.192 --> 00:00:44.432
Validate row counts, keys, totals, and category coverage before assuming a pivot-unpivot round trip preserves

00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:45.540
everything.
